      "id": "20342129",
      "title": "Using Object & Array Types",
      "lectureOrder": 501,
      "videoOrder": 443,
      "sourceHash": "b8ed17f937378c3726936106ec9d222a4b4be233c49f8d73432be9fda3760bb5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.82,
          "en": "Okay, so we know about some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.82,
          "end": 6.1,
          "en": "essential TypeScript Basics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.1,
          "end": 8.77,
          "en": "actually the core essentials already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.77,
          "end": 11.53,
          "en": "But now let's also dive into some other key types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.53,
          "end": 13.24,
          "en": "which you'll see throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.24,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "and what you need to know in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.21,
          "en": "and that are object and array types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 20.92,
          "en": "Here we're working with numbers and strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.92,
          "end": 25.7,
          "en": "but actually also already with objects, HTML input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.7,
          "end": 28.66,
          "en": "and the HTML button element, which is inferred here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.66,
          "end": 30.88,
          "en": "is actually an object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.88,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "because we have DOM objects here in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 40.17,
          "en": "Now, we can also define our own object types of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 45.17,
          "en": "Let's say we have another function, print result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.24,
          "end": 48.74,
          "en": "and here it actually wants a result object, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.82,
          "end": 54.29,
          "en": "and it wants that object to have a val prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.29,
          "end": 58.14,
          "en": "so that it console logs result object val.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 61.04,
          "en": "Now this example clearly is not made up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.04,
          "end": 63.98,
          "en": "but it is realistic that in bigger applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.98,
          "end": 66.97,
          "en": "which are writing, you'll have functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.97,
          "end": 70.75,
          "en": "that want objects as parameters, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.75,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "So here we want an object, which has a val prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 77.51,
          "en": "Now you could add any here as an explicit any type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.51,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "to make this code work, but I wanna be very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 82.21000000000001,
          "en": "that I have an object which has a val prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.21000000000001,
          "end": 83.69,
          "en": "I also wanna be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.69,
          "end": 86.75,
          "en": "what the type of the val prop value is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.75,
          "end": 89.03,
          "en": "And for that, we can set up an object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.03,
          "end": 93.32,
          "en": "by adding curly braces here after the type definition colon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.32,
          "end": 96.99000000000001,
          "en": "And then we simply define the structure of the object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.99000000000001,
          "end": 99.95,
          "en": "So with this code, I'm not creating a new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.95,
          "end": 103.52000000000001,
          "en": "This is not a place in code where we could create a object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.52000000000001,
          "end": 108.25999999999999,
          "en": "Instead here, I just define the structure of the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.25999999999999,
          "end": 111.50999999999999,
          "en": "I expect to get here on result object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.50999999999999,
          "end": 114.663,
          "en": "I'm defining a so called object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.75999999999999,
          "end": 118.87,
          "en": "And with that here, we can then say that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.87,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "we want a val field in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 124.363,
          "en": "and well, let's say is always a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.45,
          "end": 127.72,
          "en": "Now of course, we could have more properties in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.72,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "separated by a semicolon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 135.02,
          "en": "We could for example also have a timestamp here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.72,
          "end": 139.18,
          "en": "And that should actually be of type date object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.18,
          "end": 141.64,
          "en": "The date object is built into JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.64,
          "end": 144.34,
          "en": "and we can refer to its constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.34,
          "end": 146.223,
          "en": "as a type like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.6,
          "end": 149.81,
          "en": "And now when we call print result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.81,
          "end": 153.19,
          "en": "we have to ensure that we pass in such a object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.19,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "So here I can call print result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.43,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "and pass in an object which has a val key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "which should hold a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 164.85,
          "en": "Hence I use result here because that holds a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 167.107,
          "en": "And I need the timestamp here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.107,
          "end": 171.153,
          "en": "and the timestamp can be generated with new date like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.551,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "Now here actually TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 177.55,
          "en": "is not able to understand correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.55,
          "end": 180.2,
          "en": "that result will always be a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.2,
          "end": 182.03,
          "en": "since I'm passing into numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.03,
          "end": 185.09,
          "en": "it theoretically could be able to infer this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.09,
          "end": 187.231,
          "en": "that we then always return a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.231,
          "end": 189.01,
          "en": "But to let TypeScript know that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.01,
          "end": 191.44,
          "en": "this will always be a number, I can of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.44,
          "end": 193.22,
          "en": "cast it with as number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.22,
          "end": 196.07999999999998,
          "en": "because I know that this always is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.07999999999998,
          "end": 198.89,
          "en": "With that we're passing such a object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.89,
          "end": 202.66,
          "en": "and here we're creating the concrete object as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.66,
          "end": 204.59,
          "en": "we're passing it to print result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.59,
          "end": 207.98,
          "en": "where we defined the type of the parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.98,
          "end": 211.48,
          "en": "and that the type should be such a object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.48,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "With that, we'll make it very clear which kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 216.323,
          "en": "we're accepting and how it should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.41,
          "end": 219.95,
          "en": "Now objects are nice, sometimes you'll of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.95,
          "end": 221.53,
          "en": "work with arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.53,
          "end": 223.71,
          "en": "Let's say instead of logging my results here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "I wanna store them in arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 229.833,
          "en": "So add some arrays up there, numResults,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 232.97,
          "en": "which initially is an empty array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.26,
          "end": 239.26,
          "en": "and string results or textResults, which is an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.77,
          "end": 245.77,
          "en": "And here where I generate a new numeric result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.18,
          "end": 250.48,
          "en": "I'll reach out to numResults and push the result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.48,
          "end": 252.38,
          "en": "And here I'll reach out to textResults",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.4,
          "end": 255.753,
          "en": "and push my string result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 261.299,
          "en": "And thereafter, I will actually console.log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.299,
          "end": 264.003,
          "en": "numResults here and textResults.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.57,
          "end": 269.3,
          "en": "Now, you'll already see that I'm getting an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.3,
          "end": 274.3,
          "en": "That, the type of numResults implicitly is any array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.15999999999997,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "and that describes the problem really well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 281,
          "en": "We are pretty specific about the types of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281,
          "end": 283.52,
          "en": "we accept in this function for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.52,
          "end": 287.2,
          "en": "We are very unspecific regarding those arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.2,
          "end": 290.37,
          "en": "sure, both constants hold arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.37,
          "end": 292.46,
          "en": "but we're not specific regarding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.46,
          "end": 296.39,
          "en": "the values stored inside of the arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.39,
          "end": 298.851,
          "en": "And that's something we can be with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.851,
          "end": 301.71,
          "en": "We can assign a type to this constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.71,
          "end": 304.93,
          "en": "just as we assigned it to a parameter with a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.93,
          "end": 307.35,
          "en": "after the constant or variable name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.35,
          "end": 310.58,
          "en": "And then here, we wanna set this to type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.58,
          "end": 313.86,
          "en": "but not like this, but to an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.86,
          "end": 316.03,
          "en": "And for that the TypeScript shortcut,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.03,
          "end": 318.12,
          "en": "or the TypeScript way of expressing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 320.96,
          "en": "is number followed by square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.96,
          "end": 325.11,
          "en": "This means that the type of data stored in numResults",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.11,
          "end": 327.13,
          "en": "is an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.13,
          "end": 329.733,
          "en": "And here, we can set this to string array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.91,
          "end": 333.16700000000003,
          "en": "Now with that, the push methods down there complain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.16700000000003,
          "end": 335.77,
          "en": "because result is this union type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.77,
          "end": 337.73,
          "en": "and therefore it could be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.73,
          "end": 339.69,
          "en": "It's the same problem as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 339.69,
          "end": 341.903,
          "en": "So here, we can simply tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.903,
          "end": 344.04,
          "en": "that we know that this is a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.04,
          "end": 346.76,
          "en": "and we know that this is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.76,
          "end": 350.42,
          "en": "With that everything works and we can compile this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.42,
          "end": 352.973,
          "en": "Whoops, compile this code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.62,
          "end": 355.783,
          "en": "Run it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.7,
          "end": 358.44,
          "en": "Enter five and 11",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.44,
          "end": 360.35,
          "en": "and we see that those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.35,
          "end": 362.973,
          "en": "were added to the respective arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.07,
          "end": 366.04,
          "en": "These are array types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.04,
          "end": 368.754,
          "en": "And array types are of course very important because,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.754,
          "end": 373.55,
          "en": "that ensures, that we never add wrong data accidentally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.55,
          "end": 375.433,
          "en": "to an array that shouldn't hold it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
